{"kind":"article","metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"SwiftOptimize"}],"role":"article","title":"Hyperparameter Tuning & AutoML Engine","roleHeading":"Article"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Guides & Tutorials","anchor":"Guides--Tutorials","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftOptimize\/documentation\/SwiftOptimize\/CrossValidationFolds","doc:\/\/SwiftOptimize\/documentation\/SwiftOptimize\/ParallelModelSelection"]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftoptimize\/hyperparametertuning"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiftOptimize\/documentation\/SwiftOptimize\/HyperparameterTuning","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftOptimize\/documentation\/SwiftOptimize"]]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Finding the optimal combination of hyperparameters is critical for maximizing generalization accuracy. ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiftOptimize","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" provides exhaustive grid search, randomized sampling for high-dimensional parameter spaces, and end-to-end ","type":"text"},{"code":"AutoML","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" selection across multiple model families.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"anchor":"1-AutoML-Automated-Model--Parameter-Selection","type":"heading","text":"1. AutoML — Automated Model & Parameter Selection","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"AutoML","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" evaluates candidate model architectures (Decision Trees, Random Forests, Logistic Regression, Linear Regression, and Multi-Layer Perceptrons) using cross-validation, ranking candidates by performance metrics (F1-score for classification, R² for regression).","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["import Foundation","import SwiftOptimize","import SwiftML","","\/\/ 